<comment datatype='string'>The soluble NADH dehydrogenase fragment consisting of the NuoE, NuoF and NuoG subunits represents the electron input part of NADH dehydrogenase I [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/7607227&quot;&gt;Leif95&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/9485311&quot;&gt;Braun98&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/10544236&quot;&gt;Bungert99&lt;/a&gt;].
&lt;p&gt;
The NuoB, NuoCD and NuoI subunits were thought to connect the soluble fragment of NADH dehydrogenase I to the inner membrane components [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/7607227&quot;&gt;Leif95&lt;/a&gt;].</comment>
